# Use bd merge for beads JSONL files
.beads/beads.jsonl merge=beads

# The historical-documentation index is appended to by many branches at once.
# The union driver keeps both sides' additions instead of raising a conflict.
# It works a line at a time, so the file is restricted to one-line entries and
# carries no editable prose; docs/history/README.md explains the rules and
# `deno task check-docs-history-index` enforces them.
docs/history/INDEX.md merge=union

# Test-identity aliases are append-only, one JSON object per line. A file per
# test file keeps most renames apart; two that land in one alias file — the same
# test file, or test files sharing a last path segment — still append to it, and
# the union driver keeps both instead of raising a conflict. A union merge can
# only add lines, so every state it produces is one that
# `deno task check-test-aliases` still judges: that gate fails a line that does
# not parse, an identity mapped twice, a cycle, and a file that stopped growing.
tasks/test-identity-aliases/*.jsonl merge=union

# Keep generated measurement data available without expanding it in code review.
docs/history/**/*.results.json linguist-generated=true
